               <history>
                  <origin>
                     <origPlace>[Westminster:] W. de Worde</origPlace>
                     <origDate when-custom="1494" when="1494" calendar="#gregorian"> 1494</origDate>
                  </origin>
                  <provenance type="#e"><orgName role="fmo" key="org_496">Sheen, Surrey.
                        Charterhouse of Jesus of Bethlehem</orgName><p> Annotations on margins and
                        covers by <persName>John Greenhalgh</persName>, professed monk of the
                        Carthusian monastery of Jesus of Bethlehem at Sheen (professed 1495).
                        Greenhalgh writes: <q>this boke is diligently corrected out of Latin. Laus
                           Deo.</q> See also <ref
                           target="https://mlgb.bodleian.ox.ac.uk/catalog/book_5186">Cambridge,
                           Emmanuel College, MS 35</ref> and <ref
                           target="https://mlgb.bodleian.ox.ac.uk/catalog/book_5188">Trinity Coll.
                           B. 15. 18 (354).</ref> Grenehalgh also annotated <ref
                           target="https://mlgb.bodleian.ox.ac.uk/catalog/book_3783">Bodleian Douce
                           262</ref> (see under London, Charterhouse), <ref
                           target="https://mlgb.bodleian.ox.ac.uk/catalog/book_1818">BL Royal 5
                           A.v</ref> (see under Coventry, Charterhouse) and his monogram is in BL
                        Add. 24461 and 37790 and probably <ref
                           target="https://mlgb.bodleian.ox.ac.uk/catalog/book_4001">Harley
                           2373</ref> (see under Mount Grace).</p></provenance>
                  <provenance type="#i"><orgName role="fmo" key="org_537">Syon, Middlesex.
                        Bridgettine abbey of St Saviour, St Mary the Virgin, and St
                        Bridget</orgName><p><q>This boke belongeth to Dame <persName>Jhone
                              Sewelle</persName>, Syster in Syon Professed The yere of our Salvation
                           One thousand and fvye hundreth [Monogram] In die Sancti Vitalis Martyris
                           xxviij April.</q> (fol. [a iv]v).</p></provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners"><persName>Robert Hare</persName>,
                     1558.</provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">Aldenham Park, Herts: In the Aldenham
                     catalogue but not in the Aldenham sales, 22 March and 3 May 1937.</provenance>
